  "subject": {
    "id": "document-capture-producer-contract-and-locator-diagnostics",
    "type": "DOCUMENT"
  },
  "summary": "Separate the producer's capture file from the adapter's call, give the verbatim rule a method, aggregate the locator refusals, and prefer an honest citation gap.",
  "why": "A fresh producer spent both structural returns on defects the protocol could remove. The capture template put the adapter's call and the producer's output in one object with the placeholder \"replace-with-PartialEffectiveContract.identity\"; the producer copied that shape and invented the identity. The template now shows document-population.json as exactly capture, records and supersessions, with a second block for what the parent supplies, and says the producer never writes a contract identity. The verbatim rule had no method, so all seven statements were retyped paraphrases called verbatim; step 6 now says to anchor the span whitespace-insensitively, copy the block's own bytes, check every statement before stopping, and take block IDs from the reading's inventory. The adapter reported one locator defect per run, so a capture wrong throughout cost a return per statement; it now names every non-verbatim assertion and every unknown block ID, from assertions and nothing_assertable, in one sorted refusal, reason enum unchanged. A grounding block cited a standard that does not exist, so step 3 sends an unvouched vocabulary to the none_found form; citation truth is checked at review."
}
